### Walkthrough of the API. Runnable in IntelliJ, or in VS Code with the REST Client
### extension. Run the requests top to bottom, pasting ids as you go.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create a user
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "name": "Alice", "phoneNumber": "9876543210" }

### 2. Create a second user
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "name": "Bob" }

### 3. Open a wallet for Alice (paste her user id)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ALICE_USER_ID", "currency": "INR" }

### 4. Open a wallet for Bob
POST {{host}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "BOB_USER_ID", "currency": "INR" }

### 5. Fund Alice's wallet -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/deposit
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-0001

{ "toWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "amount": 1000.00, "description": "Initial top-up" }

### 6. Transfer Alice -> Bob -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0001

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 250.50, "description": "Dinner" }

### 7. The same request again, as a client retry would send it.
### -> 200 with "replayed": true, and the balances do not change.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0001

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 250.50, "description": "Dinner" }

### 8. Same key, different amount -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_ERROR
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0001

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 999.00 }

### 9. Overdraw -> 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS.
### Retrying with the same key returns the same rejection, not a late success.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0002

{ "fromWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 5000.00 }

### 10. Missing Idempotency-Key -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 1.00 }

### 11. Balance
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/ALICE_WALLET_ID/balance

### 12. Double-entry rows for the wallet, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/ALICE_WALLET_ID/ledger

### 13. Everything this wallet took part in
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/BOB_WALLET_ID/transactions

### 14. All of a user's wallets
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/ALICE_USER_ID/wallets

### 15. Health
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
